+### Example: Atomically start a guarded idle turn
+
+Use `turn/startIfIdle` for a detached producer that must not overwrite or steer
+newer thread activity. `expectedLastTurnId` must identify the latest visible
+turn and that turn must have completed successfully. Rejections return one of
+`threadNotLoaded`, `threadBusy`, `noVisibleTurn`, `latestTurnNotCompleted`, or
+`latestTurnMismatch`. `actualLastTurnId` is non-null when the server can safely
+identify the latest visible turn.
+
+```json
+{ "method": "turn/startIfIdle", "id": 31, "params": {
+    "threadId": "thr_123",
+    "expectedLastTurnId": "turn_456",
+    "clientUserMessageId": "monitor_delivery_123",
+    "input": [ { "type": "text", "text": "The registered monitor fired." } ]
+} }
+{ "id": 31, "result": {
+    "status": "admitted",
+    "turn": { "id": "turn_457", "status": "inProgress", "items": [], "error": null }
+} }
+```
+
+A stale request is conclusive and does not submit its input:
+
+```json
+{ "id": 31, "result": {
+    "status": "rejected",
+    "reason": "latestTurnMismatch",
+    "actualLastTurnId": "turn_999"
+} }
+```
+
